================================================================================
1. OVERVIEW
================================================================================

screenwall_generator.py generates flat pattern DXF files for perforated metal
screenwall panels with sheet metal J and L flanges. The Streamlit app accepts a
CSV of panel specs and returns a ZIP of DXF files, one per panel.

Dependencies: ezdxf, csv, math, os (stdlib)
Entry point:  generate_panel_dxf(spec: PanelSpec, outdir: str)
CSV parser:   parse_csv(path: str) -> list[PanelSpec]


================================================================================
2. MATERIAL & MACHINE CONTEXT
================================================================================

Machine: Artform Wall Machine / Ermaksan Speed Bend Pro (air bending, 90-degree)

Supported lookup families (current code via MATERIAL_TABLE):
  3003-H14 Al  — per-thickness r/k table
  5052-H32 Al  — per-thickness r/k table
  Steel        — 16GA/14GA/11GA/1/4", k=0.44-0.47
  6061-T6 Al   — per-thickness r/k table, larger IR required (1.5T-2.0T)

Bend rule source:
  get_rules(spec) looks up (alloy_normalized, round(thickness, 4)) in MATERIAL_TABLE.
  If there is no exact row for that alloy family, it picks the nearest thickness.
  If there is no family match at all, fallback is r = thickness and k = 0.33.

Gauge decoding:
  Gauge strings are material-aware.
  Aluminum/default rows: 16 ga = 0.0625, 14 ga = 0.0800, 11 ga = 0.1250
  Steel rows:            16 ga = 0.0600, 14 ga = 0.0750, 11 ga = 0.1200
  material=steel is enough to drive both gauge decoding and bend-rule lookup
  to the steel table. alloy may still be "steel" (or a steel descriptor) for
  clarity, but it is no longer required just to hit the steel values.

Overrides available per panel in CSV:
  k_factor_override, bend_radius_override


================================================================================
3. BEND MATH — VERIFIED AGAINST FUSION 360
================================================================================

All formulas for 90-degree air bending:

  OSS = R + T                          Outside Setback (= tan(45°) × (R+T))
  BA  = (π/2) × (R + K × T)           Bend Allowance
  BD  = 2 × OSS - BA = 2(R+T) - BA    Bend Deduction
  BA/2 = (π/4) × (R + K × T)          Bend CL offset from hard corner

Verified values (0.1875" 3003, R=0.125, K=0.33):
  OSS  = 0.3125"
  BA   = 0.2935"   [Fusion measures 0.294" bend zone ✓]
  BD   = 0.3315"
  BA/2 = 0.1468"   [Fusion: 0.147" ✓]

Flat zone formulas:
  f2 = nominal_f2 - BD/2        lip zone (blank edge to bend2 CL)
     = 2.25 - 0.166 = 2.084"    [Fusion: 2.084" ✓]

  f1 = nominal_f1 - 3×BD/2      leg zone (used for blank SIZE only)
     = 2.00 - 0.497 = 1.503"

  CL-to-CL span = nominal_f1 - BD = 2.00 - 0.331 = 1.669"  [Fusion: 1.669" ✓]

  ex = f1 + f2 = 3.587" per side

Blank size:
  blank_w = face_width  + 2 × ex = 24 + 7.174 = 31.174"  [Fusion: 31.174" ✓]
  blank_h = face_height + 2 × ex = 36 + 7.174 = 43.174"  [Fusion: 43.174" ✓]

Hard corner / void inner corner — two datums:
  Bend theory (Fusion §3 anchor): distance from blank edge to bend-deduction inner corner
    = ex + BD (blank sizing / HC-HC checks vs Fusion still use this model).
  Shop DXF `cut` (ortho/RT): void inner corners at nominal face inner corner + CI along
    active axes (CI = SHOP_FLANGE_CORNER_INSET ≈0.195″ ref), not +BD — perimeter face→
    inside-leg matches shop coupon. `bend` layer ortho: HC quad at nominal face + BD.

Layout from blank edge inward:
  [blank edge]--f2=2.084"--[bend2 CL]--1.669"--[bend1 CL]--BA/2=0.147"--[HC]--face

Bend line positions (blank sizing / Fusion J reference):
  bend2 CL from blank edge = f2 = 2.084"          [Fusion: 2.084" ✓]
  bend1 CL from blank edge = HC - BA/2 = 3.771"   [J reference from HC ✓]
  bend1 CL from HC         = BA/2 = 0.147"       [Fusion: 0.147" ✓]  (J on DXF `bend`)
  bend2 CL from HC         = HC - f2 = 1.834"     [Fusion: 1.823" ✓]

L flange (single 90°, same material row as above):
  f1_flat (blank sizing) = nominal_f1 - OSS + BA   (= nominal_f1 - BD/2 + BA/2)
  DXF bend 1 CL on `bend`: J = BA/2 from HC toward blank (HC from nominal face + BD ortho);
    L = `_f1_bend_inset_from_face` + BA/2 from nominal face toward blank (shop F1 inset ref
    + material blend — not the same inches as CI on `cut`).

PHYSICAL DESCRIPTION:
  Bend 1 = leg fold, tight to face (small BA/2 offset)
  Bend 2 = J return lip fold (the return that forms the J channel)
  Flange1 folds 90° AWAY from face, flange2 folds 90° BACK toward face.

All differences from Fusion < 0.015" = accumulated rounding, within fab tolerance.


================================================================================
4. FLAT PATTERN GEOMETRY — VARIABLE-EDGE OUTLINE
================================================================================

The blank outline is a variable-sided closed polygon. Edge count depends on the
flange configuration at each of the 4 corners.

CORNER TYPES:
  Type A (J+J): 4 edges — void_edge, miter, miter, void_edge
  Type B (active corner without J+J): void to HC on cut when notch_size=0 — covers L+L, J+L, L+J
          Covers L+L, J+L, and L+J. A J side only gets a miter when it meets
          another J side at that corner.
  Type C (active+inactive): 1 edge  — square flange end
  Type D (inactive+inactive): 0 edges — point only

EDGE COUNTS BY FLANGE CODE:
  J4S           4 A-corners × 4 + 4 primary = 20 edges
  L4S           4 B-corners × 2 + 4 primary = 12 edges
  J2TB          4 C-corners × 1 + 4 primary =  8 edges
  L2TB          4 C-corners × 1 + 4 primary =  8 edges
  J2LR          4 C-corners × 1 + 4 primary =  8 edges
  L2LR          4 C-corners × 1 + 4 primary =  8 edges
  MIX J-tb/L-lr 4 B-corners × 2 + 4 primary = 12 edges

  (DXF cut outline uses notch_size=0 — vertex count tracks void+miter without the
   former 2×T corner notch vertices.)

KEY GEOMETRY RULES (`cut` layer; CI = SHOP_FLANGE_CORNER_INSET):
  J side at J+J corner:
    void_edge_length = f1 + CI
    This ensures the miter starts exactly at the bend2 centerline.

  Any side without a miter at that corner:
    void_edge_length = f1 + f2 + CI
    The path runs straight to the blank edge (square end).

  Miter only exists at J+J corners.
  Nominal miter: 45° diagonal, length = √2 × f2 = √2 × 2.084 = 2.948" ✓
  Miter starts at bend2 CL level, ends on blank outer edge.
  Purpose: allows flange2 (lip) to fold back without adjacent lips colliding.
  gap_override opens the J+J miter apex by shifting the hard-corner-side
  endpoints away from hc by gap/2 each; blank-edge endpoints stay anchored.

NON–J+J ACTIVE CORNERS (L+L, J+L, L+J) on `cut` when notch_size=0:
  No embedded 2×T square: void segments run to HC (no quadrant+bridge notch jog).
  J+J corners still use void edges + 45° miter; five-point square path is not used on cut.

J4S REFERENCE OUTLINE (20 points, CCW, blank coords with 0,0 at BL blank corner):
   1: (fx0-vl,  fy0)       BL close miter end / left primary end
   2: (fx0,     fy0)       BL hard corner (void inner, 90° inside corner)
   3: (fx0,     fy0-vb)    BL void edge down (ends at bend2 CL level)
   4: (fx0+mb,  0)         BL miter end = bottom primary start
   5: (fx1-mb,  0)         bottom primary end
   6: (fx1,     fy0-vb)    BR miter end
   7: (fx1,     fy0)       BR hard corner
   8: (fx1+vr,  fy0)       BR void edge right
   9: (bw,      fy0+mr)    BR miter end = right primary start
  10: (bw,      fy1-mr)    right primary end
  11: (fx1+vr,  fy1)       TR miter end
  12: (fx1,     fy1)       TR hard corner
  13: (fx1,     fy1+vt)    TR void edge up
  14: (fx1-mt,  bh)        TR miter end = top primary start
  15: (fx0+mt,  bh)        top primary end
  16: (fx0,     fy1+vt)    TL miter end
  17: (fx0,     fy1)       TL hard corner
  18: (fx0-vl,  fy1)       TL void edge left
  19: (0,       fy1-ml)    TL miter end = left primary start
  20: (0,       fy0+ml)    left primary end

Where (ortho `cut`):
  fx0 = el+CI,   fy0 = eb+CI    (BL void inner hard corner)
  fx1 = bw-er-CI, fy1 = bh-et-CI (TR void inner hard corner)
  vb/vt/vl/vr = f1+CI per side  (void edge lengths)
  mb/mt/ml/mr = f2 per side     (miter depths, 0 for L flanges)
  el/er/eb/et = f1+f2 per side  (blank extensions)


================================================================================
5. DXF LAYERS
================================================================================

  Layer       Color  Content
  ----------  -----  ----------------------------------------------------------
  cut         1      Blank outline (no 2×T corner relief notch; no face-corner squares)
  holes       2      Perforation circles
  fastening   5      Install slots
  bend        3      Bend 1 / Bend 2 centerlines for **L and J** (bend 2 J only)
  text        6      Panel ID stick-font linework (no DXF TEXT entities)
  finished_face 8   Nominal face: CSV width×height (ortho rect or RT trapezoid at f1+f2 runouts)

No bend_extent layer (removed). `_bend1_cl_positions` is used inside `_blank_outline`
corner routing and for bend CL on `bend` (L vs J offsets differ).

Finished-face loop: ortho `(el, eb)` to `(bw−er, bh−et)` with `el = (f1+f2)_developed` per side;
RT nominal face from `_rt_nominal_face_corners(..., SHOP_FLANGE_CORNER_INSET)` (HC toward blank
on active legs by CI). Holes/slots use this datum. `bend` ortho HC quad: nominal face + BD.


================================================================================
6. DATA MODEL
================================================================================

PanelSpec fields:
  panel_id           str    Output filename (no extension)
  face_width         float  Nominal face width (inches)
  face_height        float  Nominal face height (inches)
  thickness          float  Material thickness (inches) or gauge string
  flange_code        str    L4S / J4S / L2TB / J2TB / L2LR / J2LR / MIX
  flange_type        str    L or J (derived from flange_code)
  flange1_depth      float  Nominal leg depth (tight to face, Bend 1)
  flange2_depth      float  Nominal lip depth (J return, Bend 2), None for L
  hole_dia           float  Perforation diameter
  pitch              float  Hole center-to-center spacing
  pattern            str    straight or staggered
  fastening_pair     str    explicit install-slot sides: tb/lr/t/b/l/r/none
                             (legacy all/standard still parse)
  fastener_dia       float  Install slot width (default 0.1875");
                             slot length = fastener_dia + 0.50"
  slot_length        float  Optional total install slot length;
                             must be >= fastener_dia
  material           str    aluminum or steel
  alloy              str    3003 / 5052 / 6061 / steel
  k_factor_override  float  Optional per-panel K-factor override
  bend_radius_override float Optional per-panel bend radius override
  gap_override       float  Optional bend zone gap override
  stagger_angle      float  Stagger angle in degrees (default 60°)
  margin             float  Perforation clearance from hard corner (default 1.25")
  top/bottom/left/right_type  str   MIX mode: L or J per side
  top/bottom/left/right_f1    float MIX mode: nominal leg depth per side
  top/bottom/left/right_f2    float MIX mode: nominal lip depth per side

SideDef fields (computed by resolve_sides()):
  active  bool   Whether this side has a flange
  ftype   str    L or J
  f1      float  Flat leg for blank sizing: J = nominal - 3×BD/2; L = nominal - OSS + BA
  f2      float  Flat lip length (nominal - BD/2, J only; 0 for L)


================================================================================
7. FLANGE CODES
================================================================================

  L4S   L flange all 4 sides, same depth
  J4S   J flange all 4 sides, same depth
  L2TB  L flange top + bottom only (left/right inactive)
  J2TB  J flange top + bottom only (left/right inactive)
  L2LR  L flange left + right only (top/bottom inactive)
  J2LR  J flange left + right only (top/bottom inactive)
  MIX   Per-side type and depth via CSV *_type/*_f1/*_f2 columns

Single letters L and J are normalized to L4S and J4S.


================================================================================
8. KEY FUNCTIONS
================================================================================

  get_rules(spec)
    Returns {r, k} — bend radius and K-factor for this spec
    Looks up (alloy_normalized, round(thickness, 4)) in MATERIAL_TABLE
    Falls back to the nearest thickness within the same alloy family
    Final fallback when no family exists: r = thickness, k = 0.33

  _bd(r, k, t)          Full bend deduction for 90-degree bend
  _ba_half(r, k, t)     BA/2 (J bend-1 offset from HC; L bend-1 uses face + shop constants)
  _flat_lip(nom, r,k,t) f2 = nominal - BD/2
  _flat_leg_J(nom,r,k,t) f1 = nominal - 3×BD/2  (for blank sizing)
  _flat_leg_L(nom,r,k,t) f1 = nominal - OSS + BA  (= nominal - BD/2 + BA/2)
  resolve_sides(spec)   Returns dict of SideDef per side (top/bottom/left/right)
  _side_extra(sd)       f1+f2 per side — used for blank extension calculation
  flat_size(spec)       Returns (blank_w, blank_h)

  _nominal_finished_face_rect_xy(bw, bh, sides)
    Returns (ffx0, ffy0, ffx1, ffy1) — CSV face_width × face_height at f1+f2 runouts

  _rt_nominal_face_corners(bl, br, tr, tl, sides, hc_to_face_pad)
    RT nominal face quad (HC shifted toward blank by hc_to_face_pad on active legs;
    generate_panel_dxf passes SHOP_FLANGE_CORNER_INSET)

  _blank_outline(bw, bh, sides, bd, ba2, notch_size, gap=0.0)
    Returns CCW polygon point list (variable length by flange config + relief)
    notch_size: DXF generator passes 0 (no 2×T corner notch); gap: J+J miter apex only
    Uses `_bend1_cl_positions` for corner routing inside this polygon

  _hole_centers(face_x, face_y, face_w, face_h, hole_dia, pitch, pattern,
                stagger_angle, margin)
    Returns list of (x, y) perforation centers (call with finished-face origin/size)

  _draw_fastening_slots(msp, spec, ffx0, ffy0, ffx1, ffy1, face_w, face_h,
                        sides, blank_w, blank_h, bd)
    Draws install slots on fastening layer. J lip: nominal F2 shop offset, outer perf line,
    ≤12" o.c., J+J trim (`_j_slot_normal_ortho`, `_j_slot_stations_along_flange`). L: `_l_positions`.

  _draw_panel_id_text(doc, msp, spec, sides, ff_edge, face_holes, ...)
    Panel ID stick-font on text layer; clears slots when ID side has fastening

  generate_panel_dxf(spec, outdir)
    Main entry point. Creates DXF and saves to outdir/panel_id.dxf

  parse_csv(path)
    Parses CSV file, returns list[PanelSpec]
    Normalizes headers (lowercase, strip whitespace)
    Gauge strings: steel rows use Section 2 decimals ("16 ga"=0.0600, "14 ga"=0.0750,
    "11 ga"=0.1200). Aluminum (default material) uses nominal sheet decimals
    ("16 ga"=0.0625, "14 ga"=0.0800, "11 ga"=0.1250).

  nest_panels(panels, sw, sh)   Stub — returns [] (nesting not implemented)
  write_nesting_dxf(sheets, outdir)  Stub — returns None


================================================================================
9. CSV FORMAT
================================================================================

Required: panel_id, width, height, thickness, flange_code, flange1_depth,
          hole_diameter, hole_pitch, pattern, fastening_pair

Optional: flange2_depth, fastener_dia, slot_length, alloy, material,
          k_factor_override, bend_radius_override, gap_override,
          stagger_angle, margin

Required user-choice field: fastening_pair
  Use tb / lr / t / b / l / r / none to explicitly choose which flanges
  receive install slots. Typical practice is the long sides only.
  Legacy all / standard still parse but are not preferred.

MIX columns: top_type, top_f1, top_f2, bottom_type, bottom_f1, bottom_f2,
             left_type, left_f1, left_f2, right_type, right_f1, right_f2

Thickness: decimal inches (0.060, 0.075, 0.120 for sheet steel per Section 2;
           0.0625, 0.080, 0.125, 0.1875, 0.250 typical aluminum)
           or gauge string ("16 ga", "14 ga", "11 ga"). Gauge decoding uses steel
           decimals when `material` or `alloy` contains "steel"; otherwise aluminum
           nominal decimals (16 ga→0.0625", etc.).
Pattern: straight or staggered
Fastening_pair: tb, lr, t, b, l, r, none
                (legacy all / standard still parse but are not preferred)
Fastener_dia: install slot width
              current code slot length = fastener_dia + 0.50"
              accepted import aliases:
              slot_width, fastener_slot_width, install_slot_width
Slot_length: optional total install slot length
             must be >= fastener_dia
             accepted import aliases:
             fastener_slot_length, install_slot_length
Flange_code: L4S, J4S, L2TB, J2TB, L2LR, J2LR, MIX (or single L/J)


================================================================================
10. PERFORATION PATTERNS
================================================================================

Straight: rows and columns aligned, spacing = pitch in both x and y.

Staggered: every other row offset by pitch × cos(stagger_angle).
  Row-to-row step = pitch × sin(stagger_angle). Default angle = 60°.

Perforations placed within hard-corner-to-hard-corner face zone with
margin clearance on all sides.


================================================================================
11. INSTALL SLOTS (`fastening` layer)
================================================================================

Coordinate / viewing convention:
  Flat DXF is **inside face up** (perforated finished_face toward +Y “up” in plan as drawn).
  Panel ID stick text is authored for that view; on an **L** flange the ID may land on the
  leg that becomes **hidden after forming** when that leg folds outward.

L flanges:
  Slots in leg zone, centered between blank edge and bend-1 CL.
  First and last slot are 2" from the flange ends.
  Intermediate spacing floats as close to 12" o.c. as possible, but never exceeds 13".
  Slot orientation is parallel to the side.

J flanges (return lip):
  **Normal (into the face) position — shop rule:** let nominal_F2 = CSV `flange2_depth`
  (or MIX `*_f2` for that side). Let d_face = perforation center to inner **finished_face**
  edge, along the panel normal, for the hole row/column aligned with that slot. Then
    (slot center to blank OUTER lip edge, OC) = nominal_F2 − d_face.
  Implemented in `_j_slot_axis_coord_shop_ortho` / `_j_slot_normal_rt` (RT samples the
  finished-face edge at the hole). Slot center is clamped to stay inside the **developed**
  lip span (`SideDef.f2` minus half slot length).

  **Along the flange:** slot stations are chosen only on the **outermost** perforation
  row or column adjacent to that J (so a staggered grid does not interpolate to an inner
  line). Spacing between consecutive slot centers is never **greater** than 12"
  (`FASTENING_J_MAX_OC_IN`); it may be tighter when perforations require. Selection uses
  `_j_outer_face_holes`, `_select_slots_outer_line`, `_j_slot_stations_along_flange`.

  **J+J corners:** the 45° miter shortens usable outer lip before the straight run. Along-
  flange coordinates for station picking trim from each affected blank corner by **developed**
  `f2` (`_jj_trim_along_x_from_blank`, `_jj_trim_along_y_from_blank`) so the first/last
  slots remain in solid material.

fastening_pair values:
  tb              top + bottom only
  lr              left + right only
  t / b / l / r   single side
  none            no install slots

Legacy values:
  all / standard  all active sides


================================================================================
11a. PANEL ID (text layer)
================================================================================

  Stick-font LWPOLYLINEs only (no DXF TEXT / external fonts).
  Preferred side: first active L in order top, right, bottom, left; else first
  active side in that order.
  If that side is also in fastening_pair (has install slots): anchor along the
  flange at max(4" from flange start at fx0/fy0, first slot center + slot_length/2
  + 0.125"); if that would exceed span−4", fall back to mid-flange. Constants:
  PANEL_ID_CLEAR_FROM_FLANGE_END, PANEL_ID_CLEAR_PAST_SLOT in code.


